# ── Stemfer Worker — Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set each one with: wrangler secret put <NAME>
# Never commit real values to git.

JWT_SECRET=your-super-secret-jwt-key-min-32-chars
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-client-secret

# ── Gmail API Setup ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stemfer sends transfer notification emails via the Gmail API using OAuth2.
# The Worker exchanges a long-lived refresh token for a short-lived access
# token on every send — no Resend or SMTP needed.
#
# One-time setup (takes ~10 minutes):
#
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/gmail.googleapis.com
#    Enable the Gmail API for your project.
#
# 2. Go to APIs & Services → Credentials → Create Credentials
#    → OAuth client ID → Application type: Web application
#    Add authorized redirect URI: https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground
#    Copy the Client ID and Client Secret below.
#
# 3. Go to https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground
#    Click the gear icon (top right) → check "Use your own OAuth credentials"
#    Paste your Client ID and Client Secret.
#    In the left panel, find "Gmail API v1" and select:
#      https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send
#    Click "Authorize APIs" → sign in with the Gmail account that will send.
#    Click "Exchange authorization code for tokens"
#    Copy the "Refresh token" value.
#
# 4. Set secrets in Cloudflare:
#    wrangler secret put GMAIL_CLIENT_ID
#    wrangler secret put GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET
#    wrangler secret put GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN
#
# 5. GMAIL_SENDER is set as a plain [var] in wrangler.toml, not a secret:
#    GMAIL_SENDER = "Stemfer <your-gmail@gmail.com>"
#    (Must match the account used in step 3.)
#
GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com
GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-...
GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN=1//...
